  "name": "Angklung (Sundanese bamboo rattle ensemble)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sundanese ensemble of tuned bamboo rattles, each frame sounding one pitch so that players interlock to build melodies. Older rice-ritual forms such as angklung buhun and angklung dogdog lojor, played with long dogdog drums (here the generic membrane-drum card), stand beside the diatonic angklung Padaeng devised by Daeng Soetigna and taught at Saung Angklung Udjo in Bandung; Indonesian angklung is on the UNESCO Representative List.",
  "recipe": "classic modern angklung, art Music, southeast Asian branch. chromatic diatonic ensemble bright interlocking black bamboo angklung, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
